# Public site origin — used by sitemap/robots/canonical.
# The one variable that must be set: a production build refuses to run without
# it rather than silently baking the placeholder into every canonical URL.
SITE_URL=https://bridvance.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is optional and commented out ON PURPOSE.
#
# Uncomment a line only once you have a value for it. A variable that exists
# with an empty value is not the same as one that is unset: "" is not undefined,
# so a `?? fallback` skips the fallback and passes the empty string on. That is
# how enquiry delivery broke — an empty CONTACT_FROM reached the mail provider,
# which refused the payload with a 422, and the route reported a failed send
# that looked for all the world like a bad API key.
#
# lib/env.ts `envOr()` now treats blank and whitespace-only as absent, so the
# code is defended. These stay commented because copying blank lines into a
# hosting dashboard is still how variables nobody meant to set get created.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Enquiry delivery by email. Without RESEND_API_KEY the route answers 503, says
# so, and the form shows the address instead — a missing key has to look like a
# missing key. CONTACT_TO defaults to the studio inbox in lib/contact.ts;
# CONTACT_FROM defaults to Resend's shared sender, which needs no verified
# domain. Set CONTACT_FROM only to an address on a domain verified in Resend.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# CONTACT_TO=
# CONTACT_FROM=

# Shared rate-limit store. Unset, the limiter in lib/rateLimit.ts is per-process:
# each serverless instance keeps its own counters, so a caller spread across
# instances gets a fresh allowance on each. Setting these is the upgrade path.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Bot challenge. Unbuilt on purpose: it needs a third-party script and the CSP
# pins script-src to 'self'. The honeypot and the rate limit cover the traffic
# it would stop, so loosening the CSP for it is a bad trade.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Enquiry SMS, via Twilio. All four are needed together or the text is a no-op —
# the email is the path that must work, and a missing SMS key must never lose an
# enquiry. Prefix TWILIO_FROM and CONTACT_PHONE with `whatsapp:` to deliver there
# instead.
#
# CONTACT_PHONE is server-only on purpose: no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, read solely
# inside app/api/contact/route.ts, so Next cannot inline it into a client bundle,
# and e2e/secrets.spec.ts fails the build if a phone-shaped value ever reaches
# one. Never put a real number in this file — it is committed.
# CONTACT_PHONE=
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=
